Dahl was a noble of [[Geography/Ushas/Penthes|Penthes]] who controlled its duke from behind the throne, and a powerful necromancer. He raised an army of the dead in Old Penthes, kept a [[Bestiary/False Hydra|False Hydra]] there, and had an adjutant with [[Phenomena/Metals|palladium]] rods driven through his arms and legs, through whom Dahl could cast. He learned his necromancy from a dealmaker: [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Mephistopheles|Mephistopheles]].

The party ([[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]], [[People/Zugg|Zugg]], [[People/Rotok|Rotok]] and [[People/Althane/The Broker|T3C]]) came back with allies and defeated him, but not before he cast his true trump card, another gift of Mephistopheles: a spell that unravelled the [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]] of [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]]. It damaged the world past repair. Pockets of purple energy full of eldritch monsters opened across it, each with a [[Phenomena/Voidheart|Voidheart]] at its core, and the damage leaked out into all sixteen planes of Ushas's sphere.
